# OPTIONAL O2 (after S3a passes; four cards, separable): the 200 tok/s plan's W-1 arm: S3a's matrix again with the draft projections
# in bfloat16 (c2-packed-tp4-gate-bf16: QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_BF8=0). Compare the tokens committed per round (the [ACCEPT] mean, per user)
# with S3a's on the same prompts: the plan's A1 lever pays only if real-text acceptance rises by more than the drafter's doubled
# weight bytes cost per round. A different drafter changes what is proposed, not what is verified, so every arm's TEXT must still
# equal S3a's solo texts; a difference there is a verification fault, not an acceptance effect.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card S2 window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/s2 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here
# names a rig, a card or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. A placeholder in @...@ is filled in by whoever drives
# the window (the graft directory and the graft binary digest of the one-card harnesses); every other value is final.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image S0 builds from this same commit; a later commit needs a new tag.
# Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min; two arms 35-75 min (150 with a re-run). C2_GATE_JIT=record as in S3a.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset gate
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-s2-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-gate-bf16
C2_GATE_PLAN=matrix
C2_GATE_LENGTHS=4096,16384,32768,60000
C2_GATE_MAX_TOKENS=512
C2_GATE_JIT=record
